                <pb facs="1088" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1008"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eddy to Mr. Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports that the Russian ambassador has telegraphed instructions to
                    Sofia, and will do all in his power to assist; that the British ambassador
                    approves steps taken by United States officials, and that he will endeavor to
                    persuade the German and Austrian ambassadors to follow the example of those of
                    Russia and Great Britain.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
